  "question": "Background / Context\nThe project involves developing a comprehensive database system for an online bookstore, named `OnlineBookStore`. This system aims to efficiently manage books, authors, customers, orders, and reviews.\n\nObjectives\n- Design and implement a robust database to support core operations of an online bookstore.\n- Enable essential CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations for managing data within the bookstore.\n- Support complex query handling to facilitate comprehensive data retrieval and manipulation.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n- End Users: Customers who interact with the website to browse and purchase books, and provide reviews.\n- Administrators: Internal users responsible for managing inventory, processing orders, and maintaining customer records.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n1. Authors Management:\n   - Store author details such as name, biography, birth date, nationality, and website.\n   - Link books to respective authors.\n\n2. Books Management:\n   - Maintain details about each book, including title, ISBN, genre, price, published date, and associated author.\n   - Track book addition dates.\n\n3. Customers Management:\n   - Capture customer information including name, email, password, address, and phone number.\n   - Securely manage customer login credentials.\n\n4. Orders Processing:\n   - Record customer orders with order date, total amount, and status.\n   - Link orders to customers using unique identifiers.\n\n5. Reviews Handling:\n   - Allow customers to submit reviews with a rating and comments.\n   - Associate reviews with specific books and customers.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n- Ensure secure data handling for customer information, particularly sensitive data like emails and passwords.\n- Optimize database performance for handling large datasets and complex queries.\n- Allow seamless scalability to accommodate an expanding inventory and growing customer base.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0201\nCREATE TABLE `authors` (\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `biography` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `birth_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `nationality` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `website` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`author_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customers` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `email` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `books` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `isbn` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `genre` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `published_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `added_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `isbn` (`isbn`),\n  KEY `author_id` (`author_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `books_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `authors` (`author_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `orders` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `total_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  KEY `customer_id` (`customer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `orders_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reviews` (\n  `review_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comments` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `review_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`review_id`),\n  KEY `book_id` (`book_id`),\n  KEY `customer_id` (`customer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `reviews_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `books` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `reviews_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
